      "obligation": "refuter:24:2",
      "id": "pthm-cm08-moving-chart-energy-function",
      "location": "Statement, interval and curve hypotheses",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The Statement quantifies over any interval J and supplies only one-sided endpoint derivatives. The dependency def-interval explicitly includes the singleton interval [a,a], but there are no points on either side within that interval to define q'(a) or q''(a); def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral defines differentiability at c only when c is a limit point of the domain. Consequently e(a), which uses q'(a), is not specified in this admitted case, despite Proof 3.1 treating the empty-interior case as a singleton. Requiring J to be nondegenerate or specifying an extension convention would resolve this.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "6b7f30e3674ff2f9e588c5efb194af5b7934f3a1ba70ed30d877f2536cd3f70e"
